From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:08:49 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 18/68] Plutonium: object-fit and a resize cross-fade for
 <native-window>

Where a window's frame and its element's content box differ in size (the
app hasn't caught up with a resize, or won't take that size), object-fit
and object-position now place the frame. The UA default is "none" at the
top left, as before (a terminal snapping to whole cells isn't stretched);
fullscreen centers it.

crossfade="MS": a resize the page makes keeps showing the frame from before
it, stretched to the new content box, until the app has drawn at the new
size (or 500 ms passed), then fades it out over MS milliseconds. The old
frame is the window's surface at the old size, embedded by its exact id so
viz keeps it. With a FLIP transform animation on the element, the app is
resized once and its picture follows, as a compositor animates a window.

NativeWindowInfo carries the whole surface size, so a stretched surface
lands with its geometry (not its client-side shadows) on the box.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014h4c1E1y66mTWH3DAr58sR
